{# Widget "chweek" — patrols per week, grouped by type (PL·09).

   THE CHART IS THE ATLAS'S AND NOT THIS MODULE'S. The axis, the gridlines, the
   bar geometry, the colours, the legend and the height all come out of
   `atlas_chart()`; this module says only which series there are, what they are
   called, what category each wears and what the counts were
   (Uhifadhi\Patrol\Model\PatrolDashboard::weeklyChart). This was a hand-built
   `<svg>` with its own axis maths — a fourth answer to what a bar chart is,
   beside the one every other chart in the product draws with.

   THE CARD IS THIS MODULE'S. The `.c` shell and its tab are the dashboard card
   every widget wears; everything below the tab is the component's — the legend
   included, which is why the row of type chips that used to sit under the SVG
   is gone. #}
<div class="c" data-patrol-weekly>
    <span class="tab">Patrols per week<span class="src">· by type</span></span>
    {{ atlas_chart(dashboard.weeklyChart(types, typeCat)) }}
</div>
